ucn 0.4 system: Allocation level: L2 origin: stated mode: forward baseline: 14c8479 root: src
# Trial model for github.com/cosmicpython/code (commit 14c8479), the example app of "Architecture Patterns with
# Python" (Percival & Gregory). Architecture and rules as described in the book; relations checked against the code.

goal Allocate: allocate customer order lines to stock batches, preferring stock on hand over shipments
  src: book ch.1
rule DomainIsPure [pin]: the domain model depends on nothing outside the domain (no service layer, adapters, entrypoints, frameworks or ORM)
  src: book ch.2 (dependency inversion)
rule ThroughTheServiceLayer: entrypoints talk to the domain only through commands, the message bus and views, never to adapters directly
  src: book ch.4, ch.9
req AllocateLine [event]: WHEN an order line is allocated THE system SHALL pick the batch with available quantity, warehouse stock first, then earliest ETA
  refines Allocate
  src: book ch.1
req NoOverAllocation [unwanted]: IF no batch has enough available quantity THEN THE system SHALL emit OutOfStock and allocate nothing
  refines Allocate
  src: book ch.1, ch.8
req Idempotent: THE system SHALL treat allocating the same order line twice as a single allocation
  refines Allocate
  src: book ch.1
req Reallocate [event]: WHEN a batch quantity is reduced below its allocations THE system SHALL deallocate lines and reallocate them
  refines Allocate
  src: book ch.9
req OutOfStockEmail [event]: WHEN a product is out of stock THE system SHALL email stock@made.com
  refines Allocate
  src: book ch.8
convention OrmOnlyInAdapters: SQLAlchemy is used only by the ORM adapter and the unit of work
  check: only allocation/{adapters/**,service_layer/unit_of_work.py} imports sqlalchemy
convention FlaskOnlyInEntrypoints: Flask is used only by the HTTP entrypoint
  check: only allocation/entrypoints/** imports flask
convention RedisOnlyAtEdges: Redis is used only by the event publisher and consumer
  check: only allocation/{adapters,entrypoints}/** imports redis

system Allocation [derived]: allocation service
  container App: the allocation package
    code: allocation/**
    component Domain: Product aggregate, Batch, OrderLine, commands and events
      code: allocation/domain/**
      satisfies AllocateLine, NoOverAllocation, Idempotent
    component ServiceLayer: handlers, message bus, unit of work
      code: allocation/service_layer/**
      uses Domain, Adapters, Config
      satisfies Reallocate, OutOfStockEmail
    component Adapters: ORM mapping, repository, notifications, Redis event publisher
      code: allocation/adapters/**
      uses Domain, Config
    component Entrypoints: Flask API and Redis event consumer
      code: allocation/entrypoints/**
      uses Domain, ServiceLayer, Bootstrap, Views, Config
    component Bootstrap: dependency injection and wiring
      code: allocation/bootstrap.py
      uses Adapters, ServiceLayer
    component Views: read-side queries (CQRS)
      code: allocation/views.py
      uses ServiceLayer
    component Config: settings from environment
      code: allocation/config.py
    component Packaging: setup.py
      code: setup.py
